  "notes": "Duplicate-triage tool for game QA: the session's crash dump and signature sit in a persistent strip under the dark top bar, and every result is judged 'against your session' (✓/✗ trigger chips, 'Matches your dump' / 'Different:' signature, build-regression reasoning). Each card ends in a coloured verdict line (Reopen candidate / Possible duplicate / Related: link, do not merge / Duplicate: check canonical) and the top match is promoted in a pastel callout whose tint follows the verdict (orange reopen, lavender duplicate, blue related). The decision area uses option cards with a disabled one that explains why ('Unavailable: GW-31877 is fixed. Reopen it instead.') and a SUGGESTED badge; picking one regenerates a monospace tracker draft to copy, never submitted. Pill chips (999px radius) for tags/status; 9–10px radii for cards and panels; no icons beyond ⌕ and ✓ glyphs. Keyboard hints ('/' to focus search, ↑↓ to move between results)."
